"f1f49f83-41db-5881-9619-52564f75d31c" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/add "f1f49f83-41db-5881-9619-52564f75d31c" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\n\nBecause $3>0$, $|u|=3|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/3$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=2$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=2\\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"] [:db/add "f1f49f83-41db-5881-9619-52564f75d31c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "f1f49f83-41db-5881-9619-52564f75d31c" :question/answer-fields "9168c6ea-695d-5c34-9a06-19e028f21093"] [:db/ensure "f1f49f83-41db-5881-9619-52564f75d31c" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186064250 :knowledge-point/questions "f1f49f83-41db-5881-9619-52564f75d31c"] [:db/add "54529229-e39d-5828-9aaa-f10c52168335" :answer/id #uuid "54529229-e39d-5828-9aaa-f10c52168335"] [:db/add "54529229-e39d-5828-9aaa-f10c52168335" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "54529229-e39d-5828-9aaa-f10c52168335" :answer/value "3\\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)+C"] [:db/ensure "54529229-e39d-5828-9aaa-f10c52168335" :an